  "note": "parse_port_directions(behavioural_v) subset for the 69 cells puzzle.gds uses, recorded 2026-11-15 with the pre-issue-106 filter (_POWER_PINS = {VPWR, VGND, VPB, VNB}) so the swap to verilog_netlist.POWER_PINS can be checked against it: tools/sim/selftest_celltable.py asserts this map is unchanged for these 69 cells. Cells outside this set are deliberately NOT pinned: the swap drops KAPWR from the lpflow_*kapwr_* cells (issue #106, intended behaviour change). The two cells in cells_absent_after_filter (fill/tap: VPWR/VGND/VPB/VNB only) have no signal pins, so the filtered map is empty and parse_port_directions omits them -- under both filters. First taken from the volare install named in source (behavioural_v/install stay as that record). The self-test now resolves the models with resolve_sky130_models() instead of re-reading that path (issue #122): the 69-cell map is measured identical (drifted=0, unexpected_absent=0) across the volare c6d73a35f524070e85faff4a6a9eef49553ebc2b install recorded below and the ciel f6eeac7dad085ffcc829ccfd721f7b4ce39edcf7 install CI provisions -- the two use the two declaration styles issue #98 widened _DIR_RE for (bare `input X;` vs `input wire X;`), and both parse to the same port directions -- so resolving is safe, and the run prints the recorded provenance next to the resolved version. source.version is the resolver's own version string for the resolver-resolved install (klt pdk find --pdk sky130A on the recording host), not the volare commit the map was first parsed from.",
